A root component's func that *mutates* its state, hoisted onto the windows.

The other two root-component archives use `func bump(n int) => n + 1`, which is
pure and folds away before any backend sees it. Nothing there exercises the
reactivity pass, which is why this fixture exists: `add` writes `total`, so
passReactivity appends an updater for every binding that reads it, and the
number of copies it appends is what this archive pins.

A body func is registered in pkg.Funcs *and* on its owner. passReactivity
walked both, so every updater landed in the one Block twice -- pre-existing for
a func written in a window body, and once per window for a func passRootWindow
mounted on several, which is two here and grew with the window count. The
patches are idempotent, so nothing crashed and no test failed: it was simply
more generated code than the program says, scaling with a number the author did
not choose. That pass is gone and `main()` renders the component instead, so
`add__inst0` is one clone the splice made and the claim below is what holds it
to one patch per binding.

Both windows are patched, because both read `total` and the var is one cell on
a single-Model target. Each is patched once.

deny * `(?i)\bmain_?add\b` -- the spliced func belongs to the body it was spliced into, so no target spells it as a method of the component it was written on
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `m\.__n1\.SetText[^\n]*\n\tm\.__n0\.SetText` -- the updater block runs to __n1 and stops; a second block starting again at __n0 is the double injection this fixture is for
deny out/none/html/index.html `__n1\.textContent[^\n]*\n\s*__n0\.textContent` -- as above, for the page's handler
deny out/none/html/b.html `__n1\.textContent[^\n]*\n\s*__n0\.textContent` -- and for the second page, which carries the same func

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main root {
    var total = 0

    func add() {
        total = total + 1
    }

    ui.window #a(title="A", href="/") {
        ui.text(value="a {total}")
        ui.button(text="in", @click { add() })
    }

    ui.window #b(title="B", href="/b.html") {
        ui.text(value="b {total}")
    }
}

main()
